module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_type_parameter_name_borrowed_as_a_type

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// Consumer: directory-derived recurring_failure_mode.roster, projected by
// gunbc.design_ledgers.expected_design_failure_modes_md through docs_projection_gate.

// RUNG STATED BY THIS ROW, AND IT IS PENDING ONE THING. Found below the floor: the wrongness was
// silent — nothing refused, the emitted module simply carried a name where a type should be, and the
// panic only appeared at RUNTIME, in a store witness that executed the emitted code. The rung this
// change reaches is Mitigatable: the fabrication is deleted at the one construction that produced it,
// and a parallel wall refuses the symptom at the cast (quiet-bear-692's cast wall, landed separately)
// — a discipline and a refusal, which other legs can still skip, so it is not structural. THAT
// REACHED RUNG IS PENDING THE RUN: the naming specimen test.claim-adjacent Rust harness
// src/v1/stage0/tests/fold_accumulator_hof_cast_emitted_rust.rs has NO executing route on the required
// path today (v2-bootstrap runs no Rust integration tests); trigger: a `gunbc test` row carrying its
// claim. Until then the reached rung rests on a manual GREEN/RED run, not on the gate.
data a_type_parameter_name_borrowed_as_a_type: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_type_parameter_name_borrowed_as_a_type" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder,
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundBelowTheLadder,
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "first, an executing route for the red control (a `gunbc test` row on the required path carrying src/v1/stage0/tests/fold_accumulator_hof_cast_emitted_rust.rs's claim), which establishes Mitigatable; then a v2 callback-frame rule (v2.compiler.infer infer_callback_formal_frame) that reads a lambda's expected fn type from an instantiated signature and carries binder identity on the variable node, so a callee's own formal can never be credited as a call's argument in any carrier",
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a type node is CONSTRUCTED FROM A BINDER'S SPELLING — `type_variable_node(id: <the declaration's own type-parameter name>)` — and downstream rules then treat it as if the call had typed it. Two gates that look like substitution checks actually test spelling: an enclosing-scope membership test on a variable's NAME, and an unifier's first-wins binding that credits `T := T` because the candidate matches the callee's own parameter name and id. Once such a node is in circulation, every consumer that reads it faithfully propagates a name where a type belongs.",
    "WHERE IT BIT, silently: gunbc.durable_cas_file_store cas_slot_keys (dag/gunbc/durable_cas_file_store.dag:1230, `distinct_by_key(xs: keys, key: fn(k) { k as String })` where `keys` is built by `fold(xs, init: [], f: (acc, n) => acc |> list_push(n as NonEmptyStr))`). Nothing refused at compile time; the emitted Rust read `crate::std_list::distinct_by_key(keys, |k| panic!(\"unsupported cast from T to String\"))` and the panic was only reachable by EXECUTING the emitted store witness.",
    "HOW THE NAME ARRIVED (instrumented, not inferred). The empty accumulator types as a carrier with NO element child (`List`, connective NoConnective, zero children, measured), so the update leg `acc |> list_push(item)` falls through the algebraic TEMPLATE path, and the record-literal leg that builds the call's argument substituted `type_variable_node(id: <owner's uninstantiated parameter>)` into every field whose declared type named that parameter. The node carried name=\"T\", span file `<kernel:T>`, inferred TypeVariable id \"T\" — and it reached the higher-order call as that call's ELEMENT TYPE, so the key lambda's formal was framed from it and the cast had no established source type to lower.",
    "WHY IT LOOKED LEGITIMATE. Every guard at the binding point keys on names or on shape: an enclosing-declared-type-parameter set of STRINGS, a fully-resolved test, a `name == var` shortcut that reads declared formals as if they were bound. A node fabricated from the callee's own parameter satisfies all of them. The discriminator that actually works is BINDER IDENTITY — which declaration's type-parameter scope a variable belongs to — and it is only available if the carrier records it: measured contrast, a legitimate generic wrapper `fn push_one<U>(xs: List<U>, item: U)` binds the callee's T to the CALLER's U (evidence), while the fabricated node is the CALLEE's own unsubstituted formal (no evidence). Those two are indistinguishable by spelling, and two declarations that both write `T` break any name-based rule.",
    "MASKING, MEASURED (why absence of the panic is NOT evidence of a fix). At the parallel cast-wall head f178f6018025, after the stage0 mirrors were regenerated, the whole emitted corpus contained 0 files with an unsupported-cast panic and the store emitted 4 `int_to_decimal_string` uses with no panic — while the minimal fold probe still emitted `panic!(\"unsupported cast from T to String\")`. A refusal at the cast removes the symptom without touching the unification, so the control for this class must assert the TYPE, not the absence of a panic.",
    "RECOGNITION RULE: (1) never construct a type node from a binder's spelling — absence of instantiation evidence is the ABSENCE OF AN EXPECTED TYPE, and the slot stays an unsolved variable that the existing evidence gates refuse to credit; (2) never read a callee's UN-substituted formal as the expected type of a call's argument, and never resolve a declaration's parameter name against an ENCLOSING scope; (3) discriminate vacuous candidates by binder identity (the callee's own unsubstituted formal, or an unconstrained variable), never by whether a name matches; (4) a control for any such rule must include a generic wrapper, because an over-broad refusal breaks legitimate T := U bindings; (5) where a fabricated node has already been credited, the red control asserts the resulting TYPE or its emission shape — panic-absence can be produced by masking.",
    "CEILING AND ITS REASON: structurally guaranteed would mean a type variable can NEVER be manufactured from a name and no consumer can mistake one for evidence, which needs binder identity carried on the variable itself (a scope/owner identity on the node) rather than reconstructed from strings at each use site. THIS PR closes the one construction that produced such a node (the record-literal uninstantiated-owner-parameter arm, src/v1/04_infer.dag) and deletes the map that built it, rather than adding a second guard beside it. The v2 callback-frame rule is named as the next trigger: v2 self-host runs on the v1 seed carrier today, so v2's own lambda-frame rule (src/v2/compiler/infer.dag, infer_callback_formal_frame) is re-checked against this shape separately.",
    "RUNG STATED IS WHAT EXECUTED EVIDENCE SUPPORTS: no run of the fixture is on record in the gate, so the standing is FoundBelowTheLadder, not Mitigatable. The construction-level fix plus the measured masking contrast would reach Mitigatable once the fixture executes on the required path; this row is raised in the PR that adds that route.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
